

### Normal or Gaussian Probability Function

#### 26.2.1 \(Z(x)\!\!=\!\!\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}\,e^{-x^{2}/2}\)

\[\begin{array}{l}Z(x)\!\!=\!\!\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}\int_{-\infty}^{x}e^{-x^{2}/2 }dt\!=\!\!\int_{-\infty}^{x}Z(t)dt\\ \\ Q(x)\!\!=\!\!\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}\int_{x}^{\infty}e^{-x^{2}/2}dt\!=\!\!\int_{x }^{\infty}Z(t)dt\\ \\ A(x)\!\!=\!\!\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}\int_{-x}^{x}e^{-x^{2}/2}dt\!=\!\!\int_{-x}^{x }Z(t)dt\\ \\ P(x)\!+\!Q(x)\!\!=\!\!1\\ P(-x)\!=\!\!Q(x)\\ A(x)\!\!=\!\!2P(x)\!\!-\!1\end{array}\]

2.2 \(Q(x)\!\!=\!\!\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}\int_{-\infty}^{x}e^{-x^{2}/2}dt\!\!=\!\! \int_{-\infty}^{x}Z(t)dt\)

2.3 \(Q(x)\!\!=\!\!\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}\int_{-\infty}^{x}e^{-x^{2}/2}dt\!\!=\!\! \int_{-\infty}^{x}Z(t)dt\)

